Conversion of a libstdc++ _Bind object to std::function: the converting
constructor's _Callable constraint evaluates __invoke_result<_Bind&, Args...>
BEFORE any direct call.  Requires (1) [temp.deduct]/5: the partial
specialization result_of<_Functor(_ArgTypes...)> must expand ITS OWN
_ArgTypes pack, not a same-named pack of an enclosing instantiation
(function_parameter_pack short-name bleed); (2) [dcl.ref]/7: a declarator
reference over a substituted reference type collapses; (3) [expr.typeid]/1:
typeid(_Functor) in _Function_handler::_M_manager for a class with member
templates.  Third assertion is the goto-symex shadow_memoryt dog-food shape.
